@startuml poll-start
' cumin works - the claim (request the implementation) and agent runs in parallel.
' Document: poll.md, section on agent runs in parallel.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

participant "poll loop" as poll
participant "claim\n(request the implementation)" as claim
participant "GitHub" as gh
participant "Workspace\n(clone and worktree)" as ws
participant "agent.Service" as agents
participant "Claude Code" as cli

poll -> gh: read the snapshot
poll -> claim: hand over the claim list
claim -> agents: read the quota usage (minimal run,\nonly without a stored usage that is new enough)
agents -> cli: minimal run
cli --> agents: usage
agents --> claim: usage
note right of claim
  The one check before every start of an agent:
  at a quota limit (stop agent starts), no label
  change and no request (quota.md)
end note
claim -> gh: change the label to cumin/status/implementing
note right of claim
  No request when the label
  does not change (principle 3)
end note
claim -> claim: decide the branch name and the request
claim ->> agents: start the run (another goroutine)
claim --> poll: return
poll -> poll: next poll (does not wait for the run)

group another goroutine (one for each issue)
  agents -> ws: prepare the worktree
  agents -> gh: create the token of the role
  agents -> cli: start with the request and the role instruction
  cli --> agents: result, session ID, usage
  agents -> agents: log the result
  note right of agents
    This is the end of the run.
    The check is "end of a run" (wait for the checks).
  end note
end

note over poll, cli
  When cumin stops, it waits for the running runs.
  The context of a run is the context of the poll,
  so a stop ends the run abnormally (kind: time limit).
end note
@enduml
